<article class="env-corollary" id="033U">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/033U">Corollary <span data-tag="033U">4.5.3.30</span>.</a> Suppose we are given a categorical pullback square of $\infty $-categories </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \widetilde{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \ar [d]^-{U} \ar [r] &amp;  \widetilde{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}} \ar [d]^{V} \\ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\ar [r]^-{F} &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}, } \]
</div>
<p> where $U$ and $V$ are isofibrations. Let $C \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an object having image $D = F(C)$. Then the induced map </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \widetilde{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}_{C} = \{ C\}  \times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \widetilde{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \rightarrow \{ D\}  \times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}} \widetilde{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}} = \widetilde{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}}_{D} \]
</div>
<p> is an equivalence of $\infty $-categories. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      We have a commutative diagram 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \widetilde{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}_{C} \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  \widetilde{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \ar [d]^-{U} \ar [r]^-{F'} &amp;  \widetilde{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}} \ar [d]^{V} \\ \{ C \}  \ar [r] &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\ar [r]^-{F} &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}, } \]
</div>
<p>
       where the right square is a categorical pullback by hypothesis, and the left square is a categorical pullback by virtue of Corollary <a data-tag="033R" href="/tag/033R">4.5.3.28</a>. It follows that the outer rectangle is also a categorical pullback diagram (Proposition <a data-tag="033J" href="/tag/033J">4.5.3.19</a>). Applying Proposition <a data-tag="033P" href="/tag/033P">4.5.3.27</a>, we deduce that the map $\widetilde{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}_{C} \rightarrow \widetilde{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}}_{D}$ is an equivalence of $\infty $-categories. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</p></p></article>
